```
.check-field .field-error {
  margin-top: 6px;
  padding-left: 28px;
}

.check-field.has-error .check input {
...
}
```
I misread earlier: I thought there was a display block rule, but actually only margin/padding. Indeed no explicit display block for check-field error. So add CSS `.check-field.has-error .field-error { display: block; }`. Good catch. Add near line 1710 in styles.css. Since styles.css cached, bump link version query. Add `styles.css?v=2` in index. Or just rely; test needs reload. Add query.

Similarly maybe other missing classes. Let's add rule.

