Panel class is-open but computed opacity 0 and transform scale .98 despite `.chat-panel.is-open` rule. Why? Specificity/order? chatbot.css loaded after styles.css. `.chat-panel.is-open` should apply. But opacity 0 means that rule isn't matching? Class is "chat-panel is-open". Maybe the transition is still at 0 because headless virtual time doesn't advance CSS transitions? It has been 1.3s of virtual time; CSS animations/transitions may not run under virtual time or headless. That's likely. The computed style mid-transition initial state (opacity 0). If transitions disabled, the final computed should be 1. Chrome's virtual time might freeze animation clock. So panel could be visually invisible in test but fine in real browser. However, we can't confirm.

Could avoid transitioning opacity from 0 for reliability and accessibility; use a keyframe animation instead, or transition only transform? Opacity 0 initial is a risk if CSS transitions don't run (older browser, print, etc.). But standard. Still, to be safe, use `@starting-style`? Not.

Better: Use a simple keyframe animation on `.chat-panel.is-open` that animates opacity/transform from 0. Under headless virtual time, animations also may freeze, but final state? The keyframe animation fill-mode both would show initial 0 until animation clock. Hmm.

Alternative approach without opacity transition: keep panel fully opaque when open and animate only transform with a keyframe. If animations disabled/frozen, panel remains visible at transform none (default) unless keyframe applies initial. Use CSS:
```css
.chat-panel { ... opacity:1; transform:none; }
.chat-panel.is-open { animation: chat-in .22s ease; }
@keyframes chat-in { from { opacity:0; transform: translateY(16px) scale(.98);} to { opacity:1; transform:none;} }
```
Under normal browsers animates; under headless frozen at start? Animation starts immediately and may freeze at from state. Same issue. But at least if animations disabled via reduced motion, override animation none → visible. Headless doesn't set reduced motion though.

Could simply not animate opacity and use `transform` transition with initial transform none. Visual opening instant but usable. Given reliability, just show instantly with a subtle CSS transition on transform? If frozen mid-state, still okay if we don't start hidden. We can animate using `clip-path`? no.

The safest: `.chat-panel` default opacity 1 transform none; add class only for animation, but if animation frozen it might stay initial. Skip animations entirely for panel, use a tiny scale on launcher hover only. A chat panel appearing instantly is fine. We can add `animation: chat-pop 0.22s ease` with `@keyframes` from opacity .6 (not 0) and transform scale(.99), so even frozen it's visible. That solves test and real UX. Use:
```css
.chat-panel { opacity:1; transform:none; }
.chat-panel.is-open { animation: chat-pop .22s ease; }
@keyframes chat-pop { from { opacity:.55; transform: translateY(10px) scale(.99);} to {opacity:1; transform:none;} }
```
If animation frozen at from, opacity .55 but visible. But computed test would still show .55. In real browser fine. Yet why is virtual time freezing? It likely pauses animations because page load? Maybe `--virtual-time-budget` advances timers but not CSS animations. So test measurement always at initial transition. With .55, panel visible enough.

Alternatively set `transition` but initial opacity 1 and transform none; use keyframe only for a small pop from .96. Even frozen, visible at opacity .55? Let's use 0.7. But I'd rather avoid animation entirely. A clean chat panel opening instantly is perfectly acceptable. Remove opacity/transform transition from panel and `.is-open` rule; keep class for potential state. Then computed opacity 1. Maybe add a keyframe animation that only animates `translateY(8px)` with no opacity? If frozen at 8px, still fully visible and inside viewport. But 8px shift harmless. Yet panel bottom could shift? top moves 8px, bottom within viewport. Fine. Simpler: no panel animation; launcher hover has transition. Remove `.chat-panel` opacity/transform and `.is-open` styles. Keep `.is-open` for semantics maybe no styles. Could still add `animation: chat-panel-in 0.18s ease` with translateY only, from translateY(8px), no opacity. Under freeze, still visible. I'll do that.

